In the final step of the processing pipeline, the collected data for each tooth of the tool are visualised in the form of wear maps, either as a 3D representation or as a 2D planar visualisation (unfolded view of the rotary tool). The operator is provided with the capability to analyse the data and, with the support of the information system, to correct or disregard potential inconsistencies. This functionality is available at two levels: Single-tooth level:  inspection of measurement data in textual form and visualisation on the scan-acquired image; the operator may choose to disregard a measurement or manually overwrite it. Scan level:  inspection of 2D/3D wear maps and execution of automated filtering procedures, such as discarding  X % \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
